1675 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 416 0 R
/T (This project provides a data-driven approach to automated customer support intent classification by combining exploratory analysis, NLP-based feature engineering, machine learning, deep learning experimentation, model evaluation, and explainability. The findings highlight how customer inquiry patterns, character-level features, intent-specific terminology, and linguistic similarities contribute to accurate classification across 27 customer support intents. Model evaluation demonstrates the effectiveness of character-level TF-IDF and Logistic Regression, achieving a Macro F1-score of 0.9991 on the test set, while identifying classification challenges involving closely related invoice requests and account registration issues. The project establishes a foundation for improving automated customer support routing through enhanced text representations, confidence-based classification, ambiguity detection, and further model optimization.)
/E (This project provides a data-driven approach to automated customer support intent classification by combining exploratory analysis, NLP-based feature engineering, machine learning, deep learning experimentation, model evaluation, and explainability. The findings highlight how customer inquiry patterns, character-level features, intent-specific terminology, and linguistic similarities contribute to accurate classification across 27 customer support intents. Model evaluation demonstrates the effectiveness of character-level TF-IDF and Logistic Regression, achieving a Macro F1-score of 0.9991 on the test set, while identifying classification challenges involving closely related invoice requests and account registration issues. The project establishes a foundation for improving automated customer support routing through enhanced text representations, confidence-based classification, ambiguity detection, and further model optimization.)
/Pg 88 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
