2335 0 obj
<<
/Title (This project provides a data-driven approach to automated customer support intent classification by combining exploratory analysis, NLP-based feature engineering, machine learning, deep learning experimentation, model evaluation, and explainability. The findings highlight how customer inquiry patterns, character-level features, intent-specific terminology, and linguistic similarities contribute to accurate classification across 27 customer support intents. Model evaluation demonstrates the effectiveness of character-level TF-IDF and Logistic Regression, achieving a Macro F1-score of 0.9991 on the test set, while identifying classification challenges involving closely related invoice requests and account registration issues. The project establishes a foundation for improving automated customer support routing through enhanced text representations, confidence-based classification, ambiguity detection, and further model optimization.)
/Dest [88 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 93 0 R
/Next 3568 0 R
>>
endobj
